<title>USA: Lincoln National to buy back 3 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Lincoln National to buy back 3 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WAYNE, Ind. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lincoln National Corp said Friday it will buy back up to three million of its 104,661,620 common shares outstanding.  </p>
<p>The limited stock repurchase plan authorizes the company to make repurchases from time to time in the open market or through privately negotiated transactions.</p>
<p>Lincoln National owns and operates financial services businesses which provide life insurance, annuities, pensions, mutual funds, life-health reinsurance, property-casualty insurance and investment management services.</p>
<p>Shares of Lincoln National were trading up 1-3/8 to 47-7/8.</p>
<p>	     Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
